/**
 * How to Play, and the first-run tour that points at it.
 *
 * Its own catalog rather than another block in `core`, because this is the one body of text in the
 * game that is *about* the game rather than in it. Everything else here is the realm speaking —
 * a court card, a wave landing, a champion's biography. These strings step outside and explain the
 * machine, and mixing the two registers in one file is how a manual ends up written in the voice
 * of a chronicle and stops being useful to the person who needed it.
 *
 * The two active guide sections pair short instructions with actual gameplay captures. Keep their
 * button names and mechanics aligned with the screens and systems they explain. Older manual
 * keys remain for catalog compatibility; `data/guide.ts` defines what the help page displays.
 */
