  // ── The run ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  "guide.run.clock.h": "The clock",
  "guide.run.clock.b": "One tick is a season, about three and a half seconds. A wave lands every twelve of them. Every fourth wave is a Great Invasion — named, much larger, and announced two seasons before it arrives, so the warning is always time enough to answer it.",
  "guide.run.phases.h": "The shape of a wave",
  "guide.run.phases.b": "Those twelve seasons are not flat. Aftermath is what you have just won. Court is the one window in which the realm's own business may speak. Muster names the wave and lets nothing interrupt. Then the field. Decisions cluster where you are meant to be thinking and stop where you are meant to be watching.",
  "guide.run.prompts.h": "Decisions",
  "guide.run.prompts.b": "One full-screen decision at a time, two to four cards, and never a timer you can lose to. The clock does keep running underneath, so pause first if you want to read the map before you answer.",
  "guide.run.draft.h": "Powers",
  "guide.run.draft.b": "Every level the realm offers you a power. They are permanent, they stack, and each card says what it will do to POWER before you take it. Gold buys a reroll. Refusing pays momentum toward the next level instead, so declining is a move rather than a forfeit. Stacked far enough, some cards evolve into something else entirely.",
  "guide.run.champions.h": "Champions",
  "guide.run.champions.b": "Summons and court presentations bring you named men and women out of Vietnamese history. Each draws wages in gold every season, so a court larger than the treasury is a court that bleeds you. Whoever you summon is recorded in the Codex forever, and can found a later run.",
  "guide.run.conquest.h": "Taking a province",
  "guide.run.conquest.b": "Marching is one method of several — a province can also be bought, married into, sworn or subverted. Each is quoted with its price and its odds before you commit. And each one taken is a province that stops raising hosts against you.",
  "guide.run.ambition.h": "Ambition — the dial that decides runs",
  "guide.run.ambition.b": "This is the mechanic to understand. Every province taken, every power kept and every host raised adds ambition, and ambition does two things at once: it multiplies the next wave, up to three times over — and for every wave you survive while it is high it pays spoils in manpower, grain and stores.",
  "guide.run.ambition.p1": "It sheds nearly half of itself at every wave, so consolidating genuinely cools the realm down. A quiet stretch is a strategy, not a pause.",
  "guide.run.ambition.p2": "Growth is a price paid once, not a treadmill. The wave you bought passes; the province stays.",
  "guide.run.ambition.p3": "Doing nothing is not safe. The wave floor climbs about a ninth every wave whatever you do, and a defence that never grew is overtaken somewhere in the low twenties.",
  "guide.run.end.h": "How a run ends",
  "guide.run.end.b": "The capital falls, or the realm is left holding nothing. Either way you are shown the account — waves survived, peak power, provinces held, champions summoned, powers taken — and none of it is lost. It is banked.",

  // ── Screens ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
